          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %p
            There are many generalizations of simplicial type theory, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+interval"} directed interval
            is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} total order
            and thus the types only represent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+objects+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
              cubical objects in an
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            instead of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
                simplicial objects in an
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#GWB24"} Gratzer, Weinberger &amp; Buchholtz 2024
                use a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
                instead of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+total+order"} bounded total order
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+interval"} directed interval
                in their versions of simplicial type theory called
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+type+theory"} triangulated type theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cube+category"} Dedekind cube
                objects of an
                = succeed "-topos." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
