                %a{:href => "#PS25"} Pugh &amp; Sterling 2025
                use a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/01-bounded+semilattice"} 01-bounded semilattice
                instead of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+total+order"} bounded total order
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+interval"} directed interval
                in their version of simplicial type theory for
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+domain+theory"} synthetic domain theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phoa%27s+principle"} Phoa's principle
                (which is equivalent to quasi-coherence for free finitely generated algebras).
          %p
            These theories could hypothetically be called
            %em cubical type theories
            or
            %em cubical homotopy type theories
            for the internal type theory of cubical objects in an
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em simplicial type theory
            or
            %em simplicial homotopy type theory
            for the internal type theory of simplicial objects in an
            = succeed "-topos." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
            is already used for dependent type theories where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            itself is defined as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+path+type"} cubical path type
            out of a pre-defined interval.
